.TH LDS-TERMINAL 1 "2026-06-19" "lds-terminal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lds-terminal \- disciplined GTK4 terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lds-terminal
[options] [command [args...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
lds-terminal is the command-line entry point for Amanay, the Light Desktop
Stack terminal emulator built with GTK4, Libadwaita, and VTE.

It opens a terminal window with tab and split support, link detection, search,
and runtime diagnostics.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -w ", " --working-directory " " DIR
Set the working directory for the initial tab.
.TP
.BR -t ", " --title " " TITLE
Set the initial window title.
.TP
.BR -g ", " --geometry " " GEOMETRY
Set initial geometry in the form \fBCOLSxROWS+X+Y\fP.
.TP
.BR -e ", " --command " " COMMAND
Execute COMMAND through the shell parser.
.TP
.BR --tabs " " TABS
Set the tabs specification string.
.TP
.BR -p ", " --profile " " PROFILE
Select a profile name.
.TP
.BR -l ", " --login
Run the command as a login shell.
.TP
.BR --no-remote
Disable remote control.
.TP
.BR --compat-local-services
Force local VFS and disable desktop portals.
.TP
.BR --truecolor
Force COLORTERM=truecolor and TERM=xterm-256color.
.TP
.BR --no-truecolor
Disable TrueColor environment injection.
.TP
.BR --renderer " " MODE
Select the GSK renderer: auto, cairo, ngl, or vulkan.
.SH ARGUMENTS
If \fB--command\fP is not used, remaining positional arguments are treated as
the command to execute.

\fB--command\fP and positional command arguments are mutually exclusive.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LDS_TERMINAL_DIAG
Set to 1 to enable runtime diagnostics output.
.TP
.B GSK_RENDERER
Set automatically from \fB--renderer\fP when a non-default renderer is chosen.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gtk4 (1),
.BR vte (1)
